vtext is licensed under two licences, because it contains two different kinds of thing.

    The source code                          MIT, below.
    The files under ucd/                     UNICODE LICENSE V3, in ucd/LICENSE-UNICODE.txt.

The split is by what the file is rather than by where it came from. The Unicode
Character Database files are Unicode, Inc.'s work under its own licence and are
redistributed here unchanged, because the generated tables in ucd_*.v are derived
from them and a derivative that could not carry its source's terms would be a
licence problem of its own. Everything else is the source of this module.


